# Built by build.ps1 from the source beside it.
*.exe
*.pdb

# The disk library is 101 images of Akai's audio and other people's records. The checks
# read it when it is pointed at one; it does not belong in a public repository.
#
#   .\test.ps1 -Images D:\wherever
*.hfe
*.img
*.wav

# Working output from the command-line tool: inventories of whatever disks were to hand.
inventory*.csv
*programs-by-disk*

# The C++ side. Objects land beside the sources when Visual Studio drives the build
# rather than build.ps1, which puts them in a temp folder.
*.obj
*.ilk
*.lib
*.exp

# Visual Studio's own cache for a folder it has been asked to open. Some of it is held
# open while the IDE is running, so git cannot even read it to decide.
.vs/

# CMake's build tree for the plugin, and JUCE's compiled artefacts inside it.
Plugin/build/

# The compiled installer. Built by Installer\build-installer.ps1 from the sources beside it.
Installer/Output/

# The icon, built from Icon\*.svg by Icon\build-icon.ps1. A binary nobody can diff drifts
# from the drawing it came from; the drawings are the source and these are made from them,
# on a developer's machine and again in CI.
Icon/AkaiS950.ico
Icon/icon-1024.png
Icon/icon-128.png

# Disk images written into the installer at packaging time by AkaiS950Synth.
Installer/staging/

# The SDK's build tree. build.ps1 drives csc directly and writes one exe, but the csproj
# files are there for an IDE, and `dotnet build` puts its intermediates here.
bin/
obj/

# vscode seetings
.vscode/

# demo-mode recordings (Plugin/Demo/record-demo.ps1)
Plugin/Demo/out/
